; source-lens-int64-leaf-band.bml — a plain number past the 32-bit ceiling crosses the source lens.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
;
; A trivial int is content-addressed into the NodeID's 32-bit inst slot while it fits there.
; Past that ceiling a kernel moves it into an overflow table and the leaf wears a SECOND type
; (5 beside 1) for the same integer, decoding back to the same int64 either way — so arithmetic
; never sees the split. fsc-source-emit-leaf did, because it dispatches on the type, and it
; refused: "source-emit: leaf of unknown node_type 5". A band carrying any literal past 2^31
; could not cross the source lens at all, and said so only on the arm that splits.
;
; Found 2026-09-10 by rag-crossfade-band, whose declared rule folds to 501009504543. The heal is
; one arm in form-stdlib/source-compiler.fk; this band is the guard that keeps it.
;
; The literals below are the boundary itself, read as arithmetic rather than asserted:
;   2147483647   the last value that fits (2^31 - 1)
;   2147483648   the first that does not
;   501009504543 the rule seal that found it
;   -2147483649  one past the floor, on the other side
;
; Verdict 31 when the lens carries all of them and the boundary is where it is said to be.
section [form.bml] {
    def slil-last-inline() = 2147483647;
    def slil-first-overflow() = 2147483648;
    def slil-seal() = 501009504543;
    def slil-below-floor() = -2147483649;
    def slil-bit(ok, weight) = if ok then weight else 0;
    sum(list(
        slil-bit(eq(slil-last-inline(), 2147483647), 1),
        slil-bit(eq(slil-first-overflow(), 2147483648), 2),
        slil-bit(eq(slil-seal(), 501009504543), 4),
        slil-bit(eq(slil-below-floor(), -2147483649), 8),
        slil-bit(eq(sub(slil-first-overflow(), slil-last-inline()), 1), 16)
    ));
}
